      "totalDuration": "3 yrs 5 mos",
      "description": "Researched in applications of mathematical logic to artificial intelligence and computer science, in particular, knowledge representation and reasoning, logic programming, answer set programming, commonsense reasoning, nonmonotonic reasoning, and computational semantics of natural language.\n\n\nDeveloped a system ECASP that turns circumscriptive event calculus in terms of first-order logic into answer set programming based on the stable model semantics, so that we are able to compute event calculus reasoning with answer set solvers.\nResponsibilities \n•\tDeveloped the system using C++ and VNC 4.1.\n•\tCreated logic program encodings of domain independent axioms using AnsProlog.\n•\tCompared with the performance of other existing systems in RedHat Enterprise Linux 4.\n•\tDeveloped format-output system in C++ for a more readable output format from an answer set solver.\n•\tUsed CVS for version control of files.\n*System ECASP: An implementation of the Event Calculus as Answer Set Programming, available at \n                             http://reasoning.eas.asu.edu/ecasp/.\n\n\nDeveloped a tutoring system for foreigners to learn Korean honorifics. The system provides with proper speech levels between the speaker and the listener based on social factors such as gender, age, intimacy, formality, social rank and kinship. \nResponsibilities \n•\tBuilt an answer set programming knowledge base for speech levels in Korean honorification using AnsProlog and VNC 4.1.\n•\tDesigned file data access for the cross-platform development between AnsProlog and Java.\n•\tImplemented the state of the art Java GUI for a Windows application.\n•\tUsed SVN for version control of files.",
